{
 "about": "Write-kind scenarios of tools/goldens/scenario_results.py (wr1 t05): each runs a test program so that it writes its outputs into <out> instead of over the tracked goldens, for the parent-versus-commit diff of tools/goldens/behaviour_check.py. Fields: name; row (docs/status/golden-inventory.md); test (ctest entry giving the program and working directory); args (<src>, <build>, <out> placeholders); goldens (tracked files covered, one per output); outputs (files written into <out>, default the goldens' file names); extra (more outputs that replace no golden, e.g. the run's CRC log); system (the column a non-CRC output difference is charged to; Behaviour: names it); needs (foc, gpu); env; drop (globs of written files that are not results); ignore (regexes of text lines not compared); nightly (left out of the landing check, run by the nightly gate); systems (output -> system, overrides system); key_paths (repo paths outside engine/ the result depends on); fingerprint (args of a command whose output is an input identity, e.g. the installed mod's data); agreement (false: the stored golden is also regenerated for input updates no code diff shows, so the expand-phase agreement check does not apply).",
